# Science Is a Strong-Link Problem

![rw-book-cover](https://ueberschriften.de/favicon.ico)

## Metadata
- Author: [[Adam Mastroianni]]
- Full Title: Science Is a Strong-Link Problem
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: The text discusses the concept of strong-link and weak-link problems in various domains, including science. Strong-link problems require focusing on the best quality, while weak-link problems involve improving the weakest components. The author argues that treating science like a weak-link problem, through practices like peer review, may hinder major scientific breakthroughs.
- URL: https://www.experimental-history.com/p/science-is-a-strong-link-problem

## Highlights
- Weak-link problems are problems where the overall quality depends on how good the *worst* stuff is. You fix weak-link problems by making the weakest links stronger, or by eliminating them entirely. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hysmghh0km51f8ttv86cnr9a))
- Some problems are strong-link problems: overall quality depends on how good the *best* stuff is, and the bad stuff barely matters. Like music, for instance. You listen to the stuff you like the most and ignore the rest. When your favorite band releases a new album, you go “yippee!” When a band you’ve never heard of and wouldn’t like anyway releases a new album, you go…nothing at all, you don’t even know it’s happened. At worst, bad music makes it a little harder for you to find good music, or it annoys you by being played on the radio in the grocery store while you’re trying to buy your beetle-free asparagus. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hysmk2mtjt6yz7n50gc2q45r))
- they’re just harder to spot. Winning the Olympics is a strong-link problem: all that matters is how good your country’s *best* athletes are. Friendships are a strong-link problem: you wouldn’t trade your ride-or-dies for better acquaintances. Venture capital is a strong-link problem: it’s fine to invest in a bunch of startups that go bust as long as one of them goes to a billion. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01hysmmbg4artdt0sft3g7w3kc))
